('P', '**Cognitive-behavioral work with DSED: how it is used** (Zeanah et al., 2016):'),
('B', '**Teach and practice boundaries:** "safe adults" versus strangers, asking a parent first, staying close in public, and appropriate greetings (a wave or handshake rather than a hug), with role-play and praise.'),
('B', '**Identify and challenge caregiver beliefs:** "He’s just very friendly," "She doesn’t need me," "If he really loved us, he wouldn’t go to strangers."'),
