('P', '**Related evidence.** Across 49 studies, positive religious coping went with better adjustment to stress and negative religious coping with worse (Ano & Vasconcelles, 2005). Across 97 outcome studies, therapy adapted to clients’ religious beliefs worked about as well as standard therapy for distress and added spiritual benefits (Captari et al., 2018).'),
('P', '**Honest summary for teaching:**'),
('N', 'A stable, sensitive family, early placement, caregiver-focused work, and boundary teaching are the best available approach. Faith integration supports them; it does not replace them.'),
